// THE OTHER MODULE, AND IT IS CORRECT ON DISK.
//
// The test's second BUFFER is the one with a fault in it, and the
// difference is not a preference: `tests/run.py` compiles every file it
// stages, so a module that is wrong on disk fails the test before the
// test runs. Every wrong program in this suite therefore has to arrive
// through the overlay — which is what an editor does anyway.
Point* = {
    x*: i32,
    y*: i32,
}
